      "sha256": "735c89e05b587497c92fa6ebac3eef7731938fab60576b8b6e6fe6871f5afb5b"
    },
    "motivations": "The immense power concentrated in big corporations and governments profoundly shapes our lives—for better and for worse. Yet nearly every downside traces back to the same root: the erosion of individual agency and freedom.\n\nRestoring and securing our freedoms is what motivates me. Cut out the middlemen. Rebuild trust with transparency. Return real power to the people.\n\n",
    "objectives": "Transparency, Growth, Adoption, and Efficiency ",
    "qualifications": "I’m an engineer, a father, a family man, a business owner, and an optimist—fair-minded, level-headed, and driven by hard work. My hope is to represent the many in the Cardano community who value uncompromising integrity, deep commitment, and unflinching truth. Every decision has trade-offs, and I intend to make the ones that stay true to the principles I live by. With a background in engineering, economics, monetary policy, social systems, mathematics, and history, I’m committed to approaching governance logical and effectively. I am committed to keeping Cardano decentralized and secure while ensuring it remains scalable and interoperable—for the long haul.",
    "references": [
      {
        "@type": "Link",
        "label": "Daily thoughts",
        "uri": "https://x.com/ada_ddy"
      }
    ]
